[{:db/id 17592186221443 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d180264d-6aaf-5aca-a8a3-12aea15eb407" "question-4886c497-1cb0-54c5-b33a-8a4433090897"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fc8861f3-8c91-59c6-b70f-78e5364379e8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d180264d-6aaf-5aca-a8a3-12aea15eb407" :question/id #uuid "d180264d-6aaf-5aca-a8a3-12aea15eb407" :question/math-academy-id "q-341785" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe constant coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={cos}^{2}⁡(x)$ and $L=4,$ the constant coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant term of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=4$ and $f(x)={cos}^{2}⁡(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35410282-5f4b-5357-9a5d-9ff9a6fd0203" "answer-field-20188161-12bf-54c3-b2b9-4680bbcd0ad2" "answer-field-845d70ad-1177-56e1-8df0-09490c06c593" "answer-field-973bb348-68db-5f8b-b078-a1a0c39d3c7a" "answer-field-e5dac63d-6b9e-5dfb-b42e-18dabc9a7e34"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35410282-5f4b-5357-9a5d-9ff9a6fd0203" :answer-field/id #uuid "35410282-5f4b-5357-9a5d-9ff9a6fd0203" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e9469e8c-51e0-5224-96fa-a75a28e74c33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-268a6a72-c6bb-5269-8709-c6c7da175bb4" "answer-302071a9-c016-5db4-bb05-23cc63f79b77" "answer-e9469e8c-51e0-5224-96fa-a75a28e74c33" "answer-f29c96f1-60c0-5e30-acbf-f503ea08227b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-268a6a72-c6bb-5269-8709-c6c7da175bb4" :answer/id #uuid "268a6a72-c6bb-5269-8709-c6c7da175bb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{L}{n\\pi }x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-302071a9-c016-5db4-b